Agreed with the maintainer 2026-10-13. A repo that keeps its skills outside skills/<name>/ offers nothing today: NousResearch/hermes-agent has skills/<category>/<name>/SKILL.md (58 skills, 12 categories) and optional-skills/<category>/[<sub>/]<name>/SKILL.md (155 more), no .claude-plugin/plugin.json. scan() reads skills/ one level deep and skips a directory without SKILL.md (src/catalog.ts:179), so `skilletor available` is empty, without an error (measured on a local replica of the layout).

Wanted: an optional "path" on a source entry, a string or an array of strings, relative to the source root:

    "hermes": { "git": "https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent", "path": ["skills", "optional-skills"] }

Rules:
- "path" says where skills lie, it is NOT a new source root (no skills/agents/rules layout expected beneath it).
- Descend until a SKILL.md[.njk]: a directory holding one is one skill and is not searched further; any other directory is walked. Covers a category path (skills/research), a single skill (skills/research/arxiv), the whole of skills/ and the deeper optional-skills/ entries.
- Name = the skill directory basename. Two directories yielding one name: error, as for plugin.json skills (§4.1).
- Same refusals as a plugin.json skills path (§4.1): absolute, "..", a symlink (dangling included), missing, not a directory, the source root itself. Nothing is followed.
- "path" replaces the default scan of that source: no skills/, agents/, rules/, plugin.json or .claude/ items, no bundles — decide and say so for bundles and skilletor.json meta.
- Not part of the source identity: cache and trust stay bound to address and ref, like "ref" (§3 merging, §4.3). Say how "path" merges across project/user/local.
- Config load validates it (type, non-empty) with an error naming file, source and key (k88 style).
- plugin.json skills paths stay one level deep: going deeper there would change what existing sources offer to a wildcard.

Follow-ups to decide in the card:
- `add` of a GitHub subdirectory link (…/tree/<ref>/<dir>, refused since k119) could resolve to ref + path instead. Touches k119 wording and k125.
- The whole repo is still cloned (GitHub reports ~1.2 GB for hermes-agent, full history; the shallow clone size is not measured). Sparse checkout only if that hurts.
- Hermes target: these skills already sit in the Hermes home under skills/<category>/<name>/, so installing them for target hermes hits the ambiguous-name refusal of §16.5. Worth a README line.

Done: spec §3/§4.1 updated, catalog + config implemented with tests (nested categories, single skill, array, duplicate name, each refusal, replace-not-add), README source section, dist rebuilt. Not for branch hermes-target.

